---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About — Fantasy World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser game where you draft a fantasy World Cup XI from 100+ historical squads (1970-2026) and run them through a simulated knockout tournament."
/>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      About
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
      What is World Cup Draft Simulator?
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-secondary">
      World Cup Draft Simulator is a free, browser-based fantasy football game
      built for fans who love World Cup history. You draft a dream XI from the
      semifinalists of every World Cup from 1970 to 2026 — Pelé's Brazil 1970,
      Zidane's France 1998, Messi's Argentina 2022 and more — then run your
      squad through a simulated group stage and knockout tournament against
      the all-time greats.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">What makes it tick</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">100+ historical squads.</strong> Every team
        is rated on the same player-stat scheme — reflexes, tackling, passing,
        finishing and more — so your picks and the AI opponents are compared
        fairly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">A real match engine.</strong> Matches are
        simulated segment by segment with possession, shots, shot quality,
        extra time and penalty shootouts, tuned against real World Cup
        scorelines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">Chemistry matters.</strong> Drafting
        same-nation players boosts their performance, rewarding coherent squads
        over pure stat-stacking.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">A note on the data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      Squads are drawn from World Cup semifinalists 1970-2026. The 2026 rosters
      are fictional/predicted lineups. Ratings are game-specific estimates
      built for simulation balance, not official player statistics.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      Questions, feedback or bug reports? <a class="text-mint underline" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>